\section{Missing item responses}{

With \code{na.rm = TRUE} (the default, poLCA's default) a subject with
any missing item is dropped by the usual \code{na.action}, and the
message naming the dropped rows is the ordinary one. With
\code{na.rm = FALSE} the subject is kept and only the missing item's
factor leaves that subject's likelihood, which is poLCA's
\code{na.rm = FALSE} behavior; the mask is data, so the tape never sees a
branch. A subject missing EVERY item contributes a constant and is
better dropped.
}

\section{What is and is not supported}{

Post-fit, \code{\link[=lca_probs]{lca_probs()}} gives posterior class-membership
probabilities per subject (with the relative-entropy classification
diagnostic attached), \code{\link[=lca_profiles]{lca_profiles()}} gives the item profile table,
and \code{simulate()} draws a class per subject and then its items.
\code{fitted()}, \code{predict(type = "response")} and \code{residuals()} are
refused: the response is a matrix of nominal codes, so an "expected
item code" would be an average of arbitrary labels. Read
\code{\link[=lca_probs]{lca_probs()}} and \code{\link[=lca_profiles]{lca_profiles()}} instead. \code{predict()} itself
returns the gating linear predictor (\code{theta1} by default, any
\code{theta} with \verb{dpar =}), on \code{newdata} as well.

The gating coefficients are ordinary fixed effects, so \code{fixef()},
\code{confint()} (Wald, profile and uniroot), \code{hypothesis()},
\code{set_prior()}, \code{lower}/\code{upper} bounds and
\code{frmtmb.sample::frm_sample()} all work on
them; \code{anova()} compares nested gating formulas at one \code{K}.

Refused in this version: random effects and smooths anywhere in the
model (latent classes plus continuous random effects is the
growth-mixture shape - use \code{mixture(..., groups = ~g)} for that),
\code{REML} and \code{frmtmb_control(profile = TRUE)} (the classes are
exchangeable, so there is no single inner mode), \code{quadrature}, every
addition term (\code{weights()}, \code{cens()}, \code{trunc()}, \code{se()}, \code{mi()},
\code{trials()}), \code{\link[frmtmb:mvbf]{mvbf()}}, and \code{residuals(type = "osa")}.
}

\examples{
set.seed(1)
# four binary items measuring two well-separated classes
n <- 300
cl <- rbinom(n, 1, 0.4) + 1
pr <- rbind(c(0.85, 0.80, 0.75, 0.90), c(0.15, 0.20, 0.25, 0.10))
Y <- matrix(0L, n, 4)
for (j in 1:4) Y[, j] <- 1L + rbinom(n, 1, pr[cl, j])
dd <- data.frame(x = rnorm(n))
dd$Y <- Y

fit <- frm(bf(Y ~ 1), family = lca(K = 2), data = dd)
lca_profiles(fit)
head(lca_probs(fit))

# latent class regression: covariates gate class membership
frm(bf(Y ~ x), family = lca(K = 2), data = dd)
}
